            <div xml:id="d196-a2">

                <pb facs="0517" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg431"/>

                <p>[The following is evidently intended as the Sultan’s ratification of the
                    treaty:]</p>
                <p>We have looked into and considered this treaty, and we agree to it and accept it,
                    and we confirm everything which it sets forth, in all its provisions and
                    articles. And we confirm the same on behalf of our heirs and those who may
                    succeed us, giving our firm bond and covenant and our faithful word to carry out
                    all that is set forth in the body of this written document, and to avoid, as
                    much as possible, everything that contravenes it, and, to the best of our
                    ability, not to transgress its provisions and conditions. In confirmation of
                    which we hereto affix our sea and our signature with our own hand this 9th day
                    of Rabia-el-Akhir, 1290, [5th of June, 1873.]</p>
                <p>Approved by the poor, the unworthy,</p>
                <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">l. s.</hi>]
                        <signed>BARGHASH-BIN-SAID-BIN-SULTAN.</signed>
                    <lb/> Written by his own hand.<lb/><dateline rendition="#float-left">Translated
                        by <hi rendition="#small-caps">George Percy Badger</hi>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1873-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            30, 1873</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
